condition_name: Soft Tissue Sarcoma
condition_slug: soft-tissue-sarcoma
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "Rare disease affecting connective tissue, account for less than 1% of all new cancers yearly. There are more than 50 distinct biologic subtypes affecting blood vessel, lymphatic vessels, nerves, muscle, fat etc in any part of the body."
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features
    features[2]: "Lumps, pain, ulcers","Features of metastases, typically to liver and chest"
investigations[7]: Trucut/incisional/excision biopsy + histopathology,Chest X-ray,MRI,CT,FBC,LFT and Serum proteins,"Electrolyte, Urea and Creatinine"
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[0]:
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[3]: Radiotherapy,Chemotherapy,Targeted therapy
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[0]:
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment[4]: Surgery,"Wide excision: complete tumour excision with minimum of 2cm tumour-free margin in all planes around the tumour.","Radical excision: complete tumour excision with muscle plane or group","Resection of isolated metastasis (metastatectomy) e.g. localized liver, lung and brain metastases; when local control of the primary lesion has been achieved"
prognosis: null